From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Application Framework - OCAF binary readers report a damaged file through
 the reader status instead of dereferencing a null or spinning

TDocStd_Application::Open on a file that is not a well-formed binary OCAF document faulted in
three places, all reached with nothing but a damaged file:

 - BinLDrivers_DocumentRetrievalDriver::Read guards its first loop with aHeaderData.IsNull() and
   then reads aHeaderData->StorageVersion() unconditionally. A file no storage reader recognises
   (empty, text) leaves the Storage_Data null, so the header is null: SIGSEGV.
 - PCDM_ReadWriter::FileFormat(filename) reads td.Types()->Value(1) when the header holds no
   FILE_FORMAT line. Types() returns a new sequence, empty when the types section did not read,
   and Value(1) of an empty sequence reads past it: SIGSEGV.
 - FSD_BinaryFile::ReadCompleteInfo loops while the stream is good and the position is before the
   end of the data section, and consumes input only in the branches for the four section starts.
   A header whose offsets name no section start (truncated or overwritten) leaves the position
   where it is, so the loop never ends.

A null header is now reported as PCDM_RS_FormatFailure with a Message_Fail line, the same status
and channel the "file has no format version" branch right after it uses. An empty types table
leaves the format empty, which the caller already treats as an unrecognised file. The section
loop ends at a position no section starts at.

Measured on 1586 generated files (prefixes, header plus 0xFF or 0x00, byte flips, wrong
extension) of saved BinOcaf and BinXCAF documents: 137 SIGSEGVs before, 0 after.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3330, follow-up to #3318.

---
diff --git a/src/ApplicationFramework/TKBinL/BinLDrivers/BinLDrivers_DocumentRetrievalDriver.cxx b/src/ApplicationFramework/TKBinL/BinLDrivers/BinLDrivers_DocumentRetrievalDriver.cxx
--- a/src/ApplicationFramework/TKBinL/BinLDrivers/BinLDrivers_DocumentRetrievalDriver.cxx
+++ b/src/ApplicationFramework/TKBinL/BinLDrivers/BinLDrivers_DocumentRetrievalDriver.cxx
@@ -144,6 +144,14 @@
         theDoc->SetModifications(aLine.Token(" ", 2).IntegerValue());
       }
     }
+  }
+
+  // A file the storage reader did not recognise (empty, text, XML) has no header at all.
+  if (aHeaderData.IsNull())
+  {
+    myMsgDriver->Send(aMethStr + "error: file has no header", Message_Fail);
+    myReaderStatus = PCDM_RS_FormatFailure;
+    return;
   }

   // 1.a Version of writer
diff --git a/src/ApplicationFramework/TKCDF/PCDM/PCDM_ReadWriter.cxx b/src/ApplicationFramework/TKCDF/PCDM/PCDM_ReadWriter.cxx
--- a/src/ApplicationFramework/TKCDF/PCDM/PCDM_ReadWriter.cxx
+++ b/src/ApplicationFramework/TKCDF/PCDM/PCDM_ReadWriter.cxx
@@ -130,7 +130,12 @@
     {
       Storage_TypeData td;
       td.Read(theFileDriver);
-      theFormat = td.Types()->Value(1);
+      // A header with no FILE_FORMAT line and no readable types table leaves the table empty.
+      const occ::handle<NCollection_HSequence<TCollection_AsciiString>> aTypes = td.Types();
+      if (!aTypes.IsNull() && !aTypes->IsEmpty())
+      {
+        theFormat = aTypes->Value(1);
+      }
     }
   }
   catch (Standard_Failure const&)
diff --git a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/FSD/FSD_BinaryFile.cxx b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/FSD/FSD_BinaryFile.cxx
--- a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/FSD/FSD_BinaryFile.cxx
+++ b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/FSD/FSD_BinaryFile.cxx
@@ -740,9 +740,11 @@
         }
       }
     }
-    else if (aPos == aHeaderPos.bdata)
+    else
     {
-      //
+      // The data section, or a position no section of the header starts at (a damaged header):
+      // nothing is consumed here, so looping again would never end.
+      break;
     }
   }

